      "writtenOn": "2018-11-30T22:57:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Add END_TAG validation here considering following case:\n\n\u003ccomponent\u003eexample\u003c/component\u003e\nassuming \u003ccomponent\u003e has depth d_c, the \"example\" is another tag with only text and same depth d_c. Without END_TAG condition, it would end the while loop. And parser would end up at \"example\" tag. And, therefore, skip other \u003ccomponent\u003e tags should have been parsed.\n\nAdding END_TAG would move the parse to \u003c/component\u003e, and the next parseComponent() could start at next \u003ccomponent\u003e again.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "bdc7d3fb4ba7191567011528d5904e4e96f7a204",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8526340_3f881061",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/TelephonyComponentFactory.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 181,
      "author": {
        "id": 1351305
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-30T22:57:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In most cases, END_TAG condition is not required here. But the XML starts with the \u003cnull\u003enull\u003cnull\u003e. The middle \"null\" has the same depth as the first \u003cnull\u003e, and therefore would break the while loop. Adding END_TAG condition here is to make sure current parsing stopping at an end tag that has the depth \u003c\u003d outerDepth.",
